# Corpus rules for ingestion, in gitignore syntax (INGEST_IGNORE_FILE in src/config.py).
#
# Paths are relative to the root of the CORPUS being indexed, not to this repository.
# These rules are applied in addition to the built-in noise patterns and to the corpus's
# own .gitignore files. A file is skipped if any source excludes it, and a `!` line here
# cannot re-include what another source excludes.
#
# Written for: fraud-mlops-pipeline at 5c288080c88f0bfec435af0093a5155baaf7f343
# (~/repos/project-to-index). Decided by the owner on 2026-11-25; see
# docs/decisions.md, section 7. Rules are anchored with a leading `/` so that they only
# match at the corpus root.

# Q2: MLflow model package; a stale copy of src/ (8 files byte-identical, 10 divergent)
# plus serialized models and a lockfile.
/deploy/model/

